{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfiVmuPDHkiCL8J8v8Q3G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HpPZ6kwvNsnVX2YnwMRLjV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_3\nSRC=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/person_specific_chance_switch_belief.py\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `person_specific_chance_switch_belief`: people still judge a sequence random to the extent their own model of a fair coin (with a person-specific belief about how often chance switches) explains it better than the regular generators (a switch-biased Markov coin, a biased coin, and a repeating short motif with occasional slips), with the generators' unknowns averaged out, the evidence weighed per flip by a fitted power of length, and person-specific decisiveness. The single change is that each person also has their own habitual leaning towards the left or the right response, drawn from a population, which adds to the randomness evidence before the choice — so when the two sequences look about equally random a person's side habit decides — addressing the critique that participants' proportions of Left choices vary more across people than the incumbent produces.\nEOF\necho person_side_habit_switch_belief > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - \"$SRC\" \"$D/candidate.py\" << 'PY'\nimport sys\ns=open(sys.argv[1]).read()\ns=s.replace('''\"\"\"Per-person belief about a fair coin's switch rate in the Bayesian chance-vs-motif judgment.''','''\"\"\"Per-person side habit added to the per-person chance-switch-belief Bayesian chance-vs-motif judgment.\n\nRefinement of `person_specific_chance_switch_belief` (described below). Single\nchange: each person has a habitual leaning to the left or right response\n(non-centred normal population, 400 slots) added to the evidence before the\nchoice, addressing the critique that people's Left-choice rates vary more than\nthe incumbent produces.\n\nOriginal description:''')\ns=s.replace('''    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(eta))''','''    # Person-specific side habit (non-centred population, mean shared bias).\n    mu_side = pm.Normal(\"mu_side\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.5)\n    sigma_side = pm.HalfNormal(\"sigma_side\", sigma=0.3)\n    z_side = pm.Normal(\"z_side\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=400)\n    side = mu_side + sigma_side * z_side\n\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(eta + side[pid]))''')\nopen(sys.argv[2],'w').write(s)\nPY\ngrep -n side $D/candidate.py | head; cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3159,"cache_read_input_tokens":64718,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3159,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b6a4f54-6d1b-4227-94f8-01fcb45253e4","uuid":"18063572-a035-4493-bfd4-a62b64701f49","timestamp":"2026-10-05T04:57:23.748Z","request_id":"req_011CfiVmu28CpyEEYCKvaEKn"}
